Implementation:
Added --refterm-source CLI parameter to segment.py with:
- Three choices: hebrew-word, hebrew-lemma, fhl-chinese
- Default: fhl-chinese (best accuracy based on testing)
- Comprehensive help text explaining independence from --semantic-engine
- Data source (what to match) vs Algorithm (how to match)

Parameter Definition:
```bash
--refterm-source {hebrew-word,hebrew-lemma,fhl-chinese}
    RefTerm data source for --use-refterm (Phase 2.3).
    Options:
        hebrew-word (Hebrew word form from FHL Parsing API)
        hebrew-lemma (Hebrew root/lemma from FHL Parsing API)
        fhl-chinese (FHL Chinese explanation - RECOMMENDED, best accuracy)
    This is INDEPENDENT from --semantic-engine.
    Data source (what to match) vs Algorithm (how to match).
    Default: fhl-chinese.
```

Test Results:
✅ Parameter successfully added and parsed
✅ All three options validate correctly
✅ Invalid options properly rejected
✅ Default value (fhl-chinese) works correctly
✅ Help text displays correctly

Usage Example:
```bash
./segment.py --chineses 創 --chap 3 --sec 5 --version lcc \
  --seg jieba --correct-with-sn --use-refterm \
  --refterm-source fhl-chinese \
  --semantic-engine sentence-transformer
```

